IF3 control-channel capture — 2026-09-05, in the car, STM32 bridge
(teslamic-stm32, --features "feature-unit,if3-log")

534 frames. Every `A5 5A` write the car sent, logged over the ST-Link by the
`if3-log` build. Captured by moving one control at a time, in this order:

  1. mic volume slider — down, up, down
  2. reverb slider — down, up, down
  3. each of the four sound effects, tapped in turn
  4. media transport — play, pause, next, previous, from both the steering wheel
     and the screen: NOTHING. Not one frame.
  5. the volume roller, down and up: frames #534-563, all cc=0x00 — the same
     control the mic volume slider sends.

Decoded in RESEARCH.md section 3.3. Kept verbatim because the decode is an
interpretation and this is the evidence: anything read wrong here can be read
again without going back to the car.

Frames are the device's view. The mic's replies are not here — IF3 has no
endpoint and the car never reads back over the control channel, so a device-side
log cannot see them. That still needs a bus sniffer.

